{
    "notes": [
        "Local synthetic Caddy HTTP/1.1 runs on one physical host with disjoint server/generator CPU allocations; no TLS or WAN. One run per configuration, not a statistical capacity guarantee.",
        "Each phase used 90 seconds, 30 writes and a halfway reconnect. Baseline is the previous compact implementation; persistent loops use the same protocol and resource scopes.",
        "All phases completed writes and initial/reconnect handshakes without HTTP/SSE errors, stale final views or failed/pending jobs. All overall gates remain false: 10,000-viewer push p95 exceeds 100 ms and no phase has live-GET latency samples because public GETs were eliminated.",
        "publication_to_compact_encode ends at the frame-construction timestamp before final JSON serialization. compact_encode_to_receive ends after SSE/JSON parsing and includes generator scheduling. These do not isolate ASGI, kernel, proxy or network time. Percentiles must not be summed.",
        "Four SSE workers did not improve 10,000-viewer p95 in this run. Production worker defaults are unchanged. Generator event-loop lag warrants measurement on a separate machine before attributing remaining delivery delay."
    ],
